<SiteLayout title="Networks" description="HonorCart's approach to affiliate-network compatibility and compliance."><PageHero eyebrow="For affiliate networks" title="Designed to be auditable." lead="HonorCart’s goal is straightforward: recognize supported network referrals, respect their attribution, and make our behavior inspectable."/><section class="section shell"><div class="three-grid"><article class="plain-card"><h3>Network-aware rules</h3><p>Each supported network has versioned signal definitions, attribution guidance, and an independent monetization switch.</p></article><article class="plain-card"><h3>Minimal event records</h3><p>Protection events retain the evidence needed for creator reporting without collecting full browsing histories or sensitive credentials.</p></article><article class="plain-card"><h3>Fast intervention</h3><p>Server-side controls can disable a network, merchant, or offer immediately when policy or technical behavior is uncertain.</p></article></div></section><section class="section soft"><div class="shell two-col"><div><p class="eyebrow">Compatibility registry</p><h2>Support is earned, not assumed.</h2></div><div class="prose"><p>Network support will move through documented states: research, testing, limited beta, and supported. The public registry will describe which signals are recognized and when HonorCart must stand down.</p><p>No network logos or compatibility claims will be published until validated.</p><a class="button" href="mailto:networks@honorcart.com">Talk with HonorCart</a></div></div></section></SiteLayout>
